  "summary": {
    "title": "Add interactive Expo bike-shopping prototype from Figma",
    "changes": [
      "Preserved the supplied Figma presentation scaffold and implemented catalog, product details, cart, shipping-address entry, and mock confirmation screens.",
      "Added session-only search, category filters, favorites, product tabs, back navigation, cart quantity changes and removal, cents-based totals, and non-stacking Bike discounts.",
      "Added required shipping-address validation and an explicitly labeled mock confirmation that creates no real order, payment, or shipment.",
      "Included iOS and Android native source, deterministic shopping-state tests, verification scripts, and updated documentation."
    ],
    "testing": [
      "Shopping-state tests passed; independent review reran npm test with four tests passing.",
      "TypeScript checking and JavaScript exports for both iOS and Android passed.",
      "Independent review passed expo install --check, 100 integer-arithmetic discount cases, and a reducer immutability probe.",
      "The supplied iOS preparation command succeeded, and the iOS Release candidate was built, installed, and exercised in the simulator.",
      "QA passed AC1–AC5, covering visual comparison with all four design references, search and filters, favorites, product tabs, navigation, cart updates, discount recalculation, checkout validation, and successful mock confirmation.",
      "Independent review found no blocking correctness, security, regression, or scope-compliance defects and freshly exercised the core shopping flow on iOS."
    ],
    "limitations": [
      "Android native execution and hardware Back behavior remain unverified; Android JavaScript export passed, and shared shopping behavior was verified on iOS.",
      "Visual fidelity includes approximations in card geometry, navigation treatment, product silhouettes, and decorative effects. Inherited low-resolution product imagery appears soft when enlarged.",
      "Secondary navigation icons remain visual-only. State is session-only; no backend, persistence, real payment, or real order creation is included.",
      "Independent review noted an advisory maintainability issue: densely formatted screen JSX and route expressions should be reformatted and decomposed in a follow-up."
    ]
  },
